# The game runs with NO configuration: multiplayer goes over a public MQTT
# broker, and without Redis the API keeps profiles in memory (fine for local
# dev, wiped on restart).
#
# Copy to .env for local development. On Vercel set these in
# Project Settings → Environment Variables.

# --- Storage (required in production) -------------------------------------
# Upstash Redis. The Vercel ↔ Upstash integration sets KV_REST_API_URL and
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN for you; these POG_ names override them if you prefer.
# Without them a deployed site cannot remember usernames or $POG balances.
# POG_KV_REST_API_URL=
# POG_KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# --- Client build ----------------------------------------------------------
# Shown on the landing page once the token is live.
# VITE_POG_CONTRACT=YourMintAddressHere

# Swap the public MQTT broker for a dedicated one (HiveMQ Cloud, EMQX Cloud)
# if the free broker gets unreliable. Must be a WebSocket URL.
# VITE_MQTT_URL=wss://broker.hivemq.com:8884/mqtt
